  "strategy": "**Optimization Approach:**  \nWe use a two-step optimization process combining continuous and combinatorial techniques:  \n1. **Frequency Domain Initialization:** Start with sequences exhibiting flat power spectra using FFT-based interpolation.  \n2. **Adaptive Step Function Refinement:** Interpolate between detected extrema in the autocorrelation domain using gradient-based optimization.  \n\n---\n  \n**Mathematical Specification:**  \nThe optimization minimizes:  \n```  \nminimize obj = (2 * n * max_b) / (sum(a) ** 2)  \nsubject to:  \n  0 \u2264 a[i] \u2264 1000 for all i \u2208 [0, n-1]  \n  length(n) is variable, with dimensions 2^{{k}} for k \u2208 Z used as architecture for representation  \n```  \nWhere:  \n- \\(n\\) = sequence length  \n- \\(sum(a) \\geq 0.01\\) (defensive scaling condition)  \n- \\(max_b = \\|a * a\\|_\\infty\\) (Madelung maximum)\n\n**Algorithm**:\n\n**1. Frequency Domain Exploration**  \n- Use FFT-based candidates for lengths that are powers of two  \n- Evaluate sequences at critical points in the autocorrelation spectrum\n\n**2. Gradient-Based Refinement**  \n- For each candidate, compute the autocorrelation gradient  \n- Use subgradient descent with adaptive learning rate focusing on the maximum autocorrelation span  \n- Apply frequency space perturbations as a fallback optimization",
